<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>

<chapter xml:id="ch03_map_representations_path_planning_astar" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Map Representations &amp; Path Planning (A*)</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>This chapter introduces common map structures and how they support navigation planning. You will compare representations such as grids and graphs, then use them to compute feasible routes. A central focus is the A* algorithm, including how heuristics shape search efficiency and path quality. The goal is to build intuition for choosing planning methods that match task constraints.</p>
  </introduction>
  <xi:include href="./sec_global_map_representations.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="./sec_astar_pathfinding_algorithm.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="./Glossary.ptx" />
</chapter>